% Two disjoint matched pairs a1 |><| b2, a3 |><| b4 on four indices: does  w z w = w  follow?
% For this pattern the walk argument needs exactly w |><| z (equivalently z a2 z = z, or
% z a4 z = z, or w b1 w = w, or w b3 w = w -- all equivalent under the hypotheses), and it holds
% in every model found so far.  Mace4 search for a model in which it FAILS; such a model has
% w != z automatically and lies outside the reach of the walk argument.
%   x * y = y x y  (= x theta_y).  Constants: a1..a4, b1..b4, cw, cz.

op(400, infix, "*").

formulas(assumptions).
x * x = x.
(y * x) * x = y * x.
(x * y) * x = y * x.
((z * x) * y) * x = z * (y * x).
(((z * x) * y) * x) * y = (z * x) * y.

% (H1)
a1 * a2 = cw.   a2 * a3 = cw.   a3 * a4 = cw.   a4 * a1 = cw.   a1 * a3 = cw.   a2 * a4 = cw.
b1 * b2 = cz.   b2 * b3 = cz.   b3 * b4 = cz.   b4 * b1 = cz.   b1 * b3 = cz.   b2 * b4 = cz.
% (H2)
a1 * b1 = b1 * a1.   a2 * b2 = b2 * a2.   a3 * b3 = b3 * a3.   a4 * b4 = b4 * a4.
% (H3)  a1 |><| b2,  a3 |><| b4
b2 * a1 = a1.   a1 * b2 = b2.
b4 * a3 = a3.   a3 * b4 = b4.
cz * cw != cw.        % w z w != w
end_of_list.
